<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('../partials/new-head', { title: 'Privacy Policy — Kidamame' , url: 'https://www.kidamame.com/privacy/', noindex: true
    }) %>

    <body>
        <%- include('../partials/new-nav', { alwaysScrolled: true, hideNavItems: false, isInnerPage: true }) %>

        <main>
            <!-- LEGAL CONTENT -->
            <section class="legal-content">
                <div class="legal-container">
                    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <span class="last-updated">Last updated: October 19, 2026</span>

                    <p>At Kidamame, your privacy and the privacy of your children are extremely important to us. Please
                        read this Privacy Policy to understand how information is handled when you use our website and
                        applications.</p>

                    <div class="legal-highlight">
                        <div class="legal-highlight-icon">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"></i>
                        </div>
                        <div class="legal-highlight-content">
                            <p><strong>Our Promise to Parents:</strong> Your child's privacy is our top priority.
                                We built Kidamame Discovery to be a safe, calm, and private space. We <strong>do not
                                    collect, store, share, or sell any personal information</strong> from children:
                                no user profiles, no behavioral analytics, no advertising, no accounts.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h2>1. No Personal Data Collection &amp; Our Privacy Commitment</h2>
                    <p><strong>Kidamame Discovery</strong> is designed from the ground up as a safe, calm, and private
                        space for children and families. <strong>We do not collect, store, share, or sell any personal
                            information, behavioral analytics, or user profiles.</strong> The app contains no
                        third-party advertising, no tracking SDKs, and requires no user accounts.</p>

                    <h2>2. Local Device Storage</h2>
                    <p>To function properly, the app saves basic application state exclusively locally on your device
                        (via standard system preferences), such as whether premium content has been unlocked
                        (true/false) and local exploration progress within scenes. This information contains no
                        personal or device identifiers and never leaves your device.</p>

                    <h2>3. Technical Engine &amp; Store Operations</h2>
                    <p>Our app is built using the <strong>Unity Engine</strong> and distributed via the <strong>Apple
                            App Store</strong> and <strong>Google Play Store</strong>. While we do not collect any data
                        ourselves, the underlying app store systems and the Unity runtime environment (configured
                        strictly in <strong>Child-Directed / COPPA-compliant mode</strong>) may automatically process
                        basic, non-profiling technical information (such as temporary IP addresses, basic device
                        hardware type, or anonymous initialization pings) solely as necessary for <strong>support for
                            internal operations</strong>, specifically to initialize the software runtime, ensure
                        technical stability, and process or restore In-App Purchases securely through Apple StoreKit or
                        Google Play Billing.</p>
                    <p>No persistent identifiers are ever used for behavioral tracking, user profiling, or marketing
                        purposes, in compliance with the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA), the GDPR
                        provisions applicable to children (GDPR-K), and Apple App Store Guideline 1.3.</p>
                    <p>Any such technical information processed by these platform providers is handled under their
                        own privacy policies:
                        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple</a>,
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google</a>, and
                        <a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Unity</a>.
                    </p>

                    <h2>4. In-App Purchases &amp; Payment Processing</h2>
                    <p>Kidamame Discovery offers an optional, one-time in-app purchase to unlock full access. If you
                        make a purchase, all payment processing is handled directly by the respective platform provider
                        (<strong>Apple App Store</strong> via StoreKit or <strong>Google Play Store</strong> via Google
                        Play Billing). <strong>We do not collect, process, or store your credit card numbers, payment
                            card details, security codes, or billing addresses.</strong></p>
                    <p>All financial transactions are governed entirely by the terms and privacy policies of the
                        applicable app store:
                        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Privacy Policy</a>
                        and
                        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
                    </p>

                    <h2>5. Platform Crash &amp; Diagnostic Reports</h2>
                    <p>We do not integrate any third-party crash reporting or analytics SDK. However, like all apps
                        distributed through the Apple App Store and Google Play Store, Kidamame Discovery may generate
                        <strong>basic crash or diagnostic reports</strong> handled by the device operating system
                        (iOS and Android) or by the app store platforms. These reports:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Are managed by Apple and Google according to their own policies and your device settings.
                        </li>
                        <li>Are designed to contain technical diagnostic data (e.g., device model, OS version, crash
                            stack trace) and are not used by us to identify individual users.</li>
                        <li>Where made available to us in aggregated or anonymized form, are used solely to identify and
                            fix issues and keep the app stable and reliable.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>You can manage your device's diagnostic data sharing preferences through
                        your device's privacy or diagnostics settings. Please refer to your device
                        manufacturer's documentation for specific instructions.</p>

                    <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
                    <p>Our apps are directed to children and are designed so that we do not collect personal
                        information from them. If, despite these measures, you believe that any personal information
                        relating to a child has reached us (for example, through a support email sent by a child),
                        please contact us at
                        <a href="mailto:support@kidamame.com">support@kidamame.com</a> and we will promptly delete it.</p>

                    <h2>7. Website Information Collection</h2>
                    <p>When you visit our website (<strong>kidamame.com</strong>), we may collect the following
                        information:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Newsletter Subscriptions:</strong> We do not directly collect or process email
                            addresses for our newsletter on our website. Instead, users who wish to subscribe click a
                            link that redirects them to our page on Substack. Your registration and email data are
                            handled entirely by Substack according to their privacy policy, and we do not have direct
                            control over this data.</li>
                        <li><strong>Cookies:</strong> Our website employs a cookie consent mechanism (Cookiebot) to
                            respect your preferences. We only use strictly necessary cookies for basic website
                            functionality. We do not use analytics, advertising, or profiling cookies.</li>
                        <li><strong>Support Inquiries:</strong> If you contact us via email, we will use your email
                            address and provided information only to respond to your request.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>
                    <p>We do not sell, trade, or rent personal information to others. Since we do not collect personal
                        data directly through our site or apps, we do not share such information with third parties,
                        other than the limited technical and payment processing performed by platform providers as
                        described in Section 3 and Section 4.</p>

                    <h2>9. Your Rights</h2>
                    <p>Regarding our newsletter on Substack, you have the right to:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Opt-out of any email communications at any time via the unsubscribe link at the bottom of
                            each Substack email.</li>
                        <li>Manage your subscription and data directly through your Substack account.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If you wish to act on any other privacy-related rights, please email us directly.</p>

                    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>
                    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time as our apps evolve or to reflect changes in
                        regulatory requirements. If we make significant changes, we will update the "Last updated" date
                        at the top of this policy and provide prominent notice if required by law.</p>

                    <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
                    <p>If you have any questions about our Privacy Policy or data practices, please contact us at <a
                            href="mailto:support@kidamame.com">support@kidamame.com</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
        </main>

            <%- include('../partials/new-footer') %>
    </body>

</html>